<rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" version="2.0"><channel><title>Personal Combined Feed</title><link>https://example.invalid</link><description>Personal aggregate feed</description><docs>http://www.rssboard.org/rss-specification</docs><generator>python-feedgen</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:28:25 +0000</lastBuildDate><item><title>Show HN: AI Compute Footprint (energy, space, water and CO2)</title><link>https://heyyeah.github.io/AI_Compute_Footprint/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;I made AI Compute Footprint to get an understanding how big the energy, space, water + CO₂ footprint of data centres running everyday AI tasks is, and how it compares with other everyday activities.&lt;p&gt;I have a feel for how long a query takes when it runs on a local model on my laptop but I wanted to understand if we are all running these queries concurrently in the cloud, how much compute is that, how many GPUs, how much land.&lt;p&gt;All the sources, confidence ranges and assumptions are listed (for inference only) on the page and on GitHub. Feedback, corrections, collaboration is really welcome!&lt;/p&gt;
